German products sell well around the  world that's great for Germany because  exports create jobs and bring money into  the country in the countries that import  German goods however it means fewer jobs  and money leaving the country when  exports exceed imports the result is a  current account surplus for several  years now Germany's has exceeded the EU  limit of six percent which is designed  to prevent imbalances last year Germany  exported goods worth almost 1.1 trillion  euros while imports amounted to only  about nine hundred six billion that puts  the current account surplus at 190  billion euros now the EU Commission has  announced it plans to take a closer look  at German economic data a high surplus  does not necessarily mean that there is  an imbalance but you do need to examine  this further and understand whether the  high surplus in Germany is something  that is affecting the functioning of  European economy as a whole there's been  growing criticism of German economic  policies one complaint is that wages are  too low low wages help make German goods  competitive but they also mean Germans  have less money to spend some economists  say higher wages could help close the  current account surplus but many here in  Germany reject the criticism they say  Germany is successful because it makes  high-quality products  you
 

